   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color:rgb(29,34,40);font-family:&quot;lucida console&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\">I hope you are all well, I am having a tricky question on how to calculate a confidence interval (CI) <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">at 95% </span>for </span></font><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">individual densities and total population from a calculated group density   ( e.g <span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:16.8667px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:black\">5.47 groups  (3.68-8.14))/sqkm, my study area was 51sqkm, and the group size is <span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:16.8667px\">16.52 (13.80-19.24) individuals. </span></span></span></div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color:rgb(29,34,40);font-family:&quot;lucida console&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:16.8667px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:black\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:16.8667px\">I think there is a way to get CI for individual densities at 95%.</span></span></span></div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color:rgb(29,34,40);font-family:&quot;lucida console&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:16.8667px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:black\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:16.8667px\"><br></span></span></span></div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color:rgb(29,34,40);font-family:&quot;lucida console&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:16.8667px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;color:black\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;line-height:16.8667px\">Any guidance?</span></span></span></div></div>"
    ]
