   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Tuyisingize</div><br><div>If you are using either Distance for Windows or the R package <code>Distance</code> to analyse your data, the software should present to you the confidence interval you request.  Here is an example from the R package:</div><br><div><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/3bbb0c81260bf/Pasted%20File.png?part=0.1.1&amp;view=1\"></div><br><div>If, on the other hand, you are carrying out the calculation by hand, then you will need to apply the &quot;delta method&quot; to propagate the uncertainty both in the density of groups and average group size.  If this is the calculation you need, contact me off-list and I can describe the calculations to you.</div><br><div><u></u><table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:top;width:1px\"></td><td><div><strong>Eric Rexstad</strong></div><div>Senior Research Fellow, CREEM, Univ. of St Andrews, Charity SC013532</div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><div style=\"font-size:0.9em;border-top:1px dashed gray;min-width:250px;max-width:400px;margin-top:10px;padding-top:4px\"><div><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">eric.r...@st-andrews.ac.uk</a></div><div>The Observatory, Buchanan Gardens, St Andrews KY16 9LZ</div></div></td></tr></tbody></table><u></u></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div>On May 7 2020, at 1:53 pm, Tuyisingize Deo &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">deotuyi...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div>"
